+// hbfix19: a staged frame (rot 0) out to the scanout buffer by rows. A deferred popup's row goes out in three
+// pieces, left to right, each scanout pixel written once: the stage's pixels left of the popup, the popup blended
+// over the stage's pixels -- computed straight into the scanout row, exactly what blit_insets would have left in
+// the stage -- and the stage's pixels right of it; the stage is not written back and no other buffer is written.
+// Plain rows go out by memcpy or copy_row_neon: HB_COPY_WAY, else both are timed on the first 16+ staged frames
+// over runs of 32+ rows with no popup on them (alternating frame by frame), the faster per row kept and said once.
+void Display::copy_out(u32* dst, u32 dst_pitch) {
